.TH ZHEN\-CLI 1 "2026-11-04" "unheaded v0.0.0-20261104152510-c303527bc1f5+dirty" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
zhen\-cli \- Interactive terminal REPL for Zhenai: vor retrieval plus llama\-server inference (ADR\-059).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zhen\-cli
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive terminal REPL for Zhenai: vor retrieval plus llama\-server inference (ADR\-059).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-history \fIN\fR
user/assistant turn pairs kept in LLM context (default 6)
.TP
.B \-k \fIN\fR
top\-K topics to retrieve per turn (default 5)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-tokens \fIN\fR
llama\-server max_tokens (default 800)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-topic\-chars \fIN\fR
per\-topic content cap (default 10000)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
disable ANSI colour even on a tty
.TP
.B \-\-no\-memory\-recall
do not show the [memory hit] line
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist
do not save this session to zhen_conversations on exit
.TP
.B \-q \fISTRING\fR
one\-shot question; print answer and exit (same as piping)
.TP
.B \-\-temperature \fINUM\fR
sampling temperature (default 0.4)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
Backends come from the environment: VOR_URL, LLAMA_URL, ZHEN_AGENTD_URL, RAG_MODEL.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zhen\-cli
zhen\-cli \-q 'what port does Akira use?'
echo 'question' | zhen\-cli
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
